WEBVTT

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:14.140
So today, I want to talk about the greatest woman I ever met.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:20.910
Smart, funny, caring, special, proper special.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:24.250
Where do I start?

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:26.310
Okay, yeah.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.370
I've mentioned this on here before.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:34.300
I'm pretty much not an idiot.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.360
I'm actually a capable guy, considering.

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:41.240
But I'm 19, and because of the thing I told you before,

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.360
I can't yet ride a bike.

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:51.190
Who says you can't?

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:51.900
Me, then.

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:53.150
We keep trying this.

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:55.130
And we'll go on trying till it's done.

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:57.850
Now, keep your eye on Grandad.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:00.790
You mean Graham?

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:02.630
Keep your eye on Graham, then.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:07.410
Three, two, one, go!

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:13.990
And eight!

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:27.080
Nearly.

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:29.790
No, not nearly.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:32.220
I'm sick of coming up here. I'm sick of falling.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:34.550
And I'm sick of this stupid bike.

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:39.320
Ian Sinclair, don't you dare!

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:51.720
Mate, you rode it for a second.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:53.200
Can you stop calling me mate?

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:57.240
Anyway, a second's not enough.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:01:59.660
You'll do it if you keep on trying.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:02.600
I just want to make you proud.

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:04.980
You make me proud every day.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.020
Anyway, you're on your own getting that bike,

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:10.620
because our train leaves in 20 minutes.

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:12.180
Come on, love.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:05.660
Hi, uh, police, maybe.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:08.510
Stick with a hammer.

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:10.450
Keep me near-side door.

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:12.210
Because you parked in my spot.

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:13.630
It's not your spot.

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:16.900
Ladies, please.

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:21.990
Q, I suggest a simple solution.

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.560
You pay for a cracked window, you pay for a scratch door,

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:26.480
and we all agree that parking around here is a nightmare.

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:29.740
But that grown-ups really shouldn't need to call the police to sort it out for him.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:36.400
Now, if we're all agreed on that, there's no need for me to take any further police action,

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:37.600
and we can all get on with our lives.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:39.020
What do you reckon?

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:44.390
I'm just saying I am capable of more than parking disputes.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:48.340
